1407
01:23:41,050 --> 01:23:42,090
Hold the phone.

1408
01:23:45,740 --> 01:23:49,340
Dude, it's actually kinda creepy just falling down.

1409
01:23:49,340 --> 01:23:50,640
Oh shit, I don't have...

1410
01:23:52,300 --> 01:23:53,540
I don't have the tank on.

1411
01:23:56,570 --> 01:23:57,790
Yeah, let's not do that.

1412
01:23:58,990 --> 01:24:01,110
But the feeling of just zincing is...

1413
01:24:02,170 --> 01:24:04,310
Giving me Subnautica vibes, you know?

1414
01:24:08,020 --> 01:24:08,900
Kinda scary.

1415
01:24:10,380 --> 01:24:10,900
Sleep!

1416
01:24:21,090 --> 01:24:22,670
I think we're on the right path!

1417
01:24:24,090 --> 01:24:25,610
That looks familiar to me.

1418
01:24:26,590 --> 01:24:27,510
Is that a torch?

1419
01:24:27,930 --> 01:24:28,370
No.

1420
01:24:30,210 --> 01:24:32,590
Don't the yellow flowers look like torches in the distance?

1421
01:24:33,430 --> 01:24:33,910
Slightly.

1422
01:24:35,250 --> 01:24:36,550
And that's... oh yeah, we're here.

1423
01:24:36,970 --> 01:24:37,530
We made it.

1424
01:24:39,390 --> 01:24:41,370
I wasn't... I was never doubting.

1425
01:24:43,410 --> 01:24:44,630
I know where I was.

1426
01:24:44,830 --> 01:24:45,650
I told you.

1427
01:24:48,750 --> 01:24:50,230
And let me see what I have here.

1428
01:24:51,510 --> 01:24:52,910
We got some experience.

1429
01:24:55,550 --> 01:24:57,010
No swamp found though.

1430
01:24:57,970 --> 01:24:58,650
Andesites.

1431
01:24:59,710 --> 01:25:02,690
Andesite is gonna have to wait until we get a better pickaxe.

1432
01:25:03,410 --> 01:25:05,090
I just wanna have looting on it, you know?

1433
01:25:05,370 --> 01:25:05,850
Or...

1434
01:25:06,570 --> 01:25:07,050
Efficiency.

1435
01:25:07,370 --> 01:25:10,130
Before I start on every single andesite.

1436
01:25:10,450 --> 01:25:12,290
I could also start blowing things up.

1437
01:25:12,410 --> 01:25:14,930
But that requires gunpowder, which I don't have.

1438
01:25:17,130 --> 01:25:17,610
Or...

1439
01:25:17,610 --> 01:25:19,050
Yo, I just remembered!

1440
01:25:19,430 --> 01:25:22,610
We also have the possibility of drilling.

1441
01:25:23,890 --> 01:25:26,770
I just haven't quite figured out how to use it effectively yet.

1442
01:25:28,670 --> 01:25:29,670
That's what I need to do.

1443
01:25:33,720 --> 01:25:35,260
I need to investigate that, actually.

1444
01:25:37,360 --> 01:25:38,520
Did I even make a drill?

1445
01:25:38,800 --> 01:25:39,500
In this one?

1446
01:25:39,540 --> 01:25:40,800
Or was that the last world?

1447
01:25:41,700 --> 01:25:42,460
I don't remember.

1448
01:25:43,940 --> 01:25:45,660
In any case, I'm gonna make it when I come home.

1449
01:25:45,760 --> 01:25:46,720
And I'm gonna grab this as well.

1450
01:25:51,210 --> 01:25:52,910
Slowly getting ready for enchantments.

1451
01:25:54,490 --> 01:25:55,050
Enchantment!

1452
01:26:10,660 --> 01:26:11,560
I'll take that.

1453
01:26:11,700 --> 01:26:12,000
Hey!

1454
01:26:12,280 --> 01:26:12,960
There's my torch!

1455
01:26:13,960 --> 01:26:14,520
Wonderful.

1456
01:26:17,400 --> 01:26:22,740
The best part about going home, after having gone north so long, is that it's not lagging anymore.

1457
01:26:22,740 --> 01:26:24,380
You know, everything's been loaded in already.

1458
01:26:25,760 --> 01:26:26,740
That's a good feeling.

1459
01:26:27,940 --> 01:26:29,160
And there's the lone tree.

1460
01:26:30,300 --> 01:26:31,420
Also called LT.

1461
01:26:32,960 --> 01:26:34,200
That's the name of that tree.

1462
01:26:34,480 --> 01:26:36,540
We will never chop down that tree!

1463
01:26:37,400 --> 01:26:37,920
BUT!

1464
01:26:38,220 --> 01:26:40,940
At one point in the future, I will set fire to it.

1465
01:26:41,660 --> 01:26:43,320
It is at an undisclosed date.

1466
01:26:43,480 --> 01:26:47,980
There is exactly one trigger in the world that needs to happen before that happens.

1467
01:26:49,440 --> 01:26:50,780
And it's actually inevitable.

1468
01:26:52,340 --> 01:26:59,040
When I do this one thing, that I will not reveal what is, then I need to set fire to that tree.

1469
01:26:59,400 --> 01:27:01,960
In fact, I need to set fire to trees in this general area.

1470
01:27:02,140 --> 01:27:03,160
Can you figure out what it is now?

1471
01:27:04,820 --> 01:27:06,040
Uh, let me think.

1472
01:27:06,980 --> 01:27:11,800
So I will not set fire to this area, but I will set fire to this area.

1473
01:27:12,700 --> 01:27:13,120
Huh?

1474
01:27:15,000 --> 01:27:15,880
Are you thinking?

1475
01:27:16,940 --> 01:27:18,000
Do you see the vision?

1476
01:27:22,460 --> 01:27:23,480
There's actually no vision.

1477
01:27:23,580 --> 01:27:24,440
I just made that shit up.

1478
01:27:25,860 --> 01:27:27,520
There's nothing deep behind it!

1479
01:27:28,280 --> 01:27:29,160
I lied!

1480
01:27:29,240 --> 01:27:30,180
I'm a liar!

1481
01:27:36,360 --> 01:27:37,160
Where's my home?

1482
01:27:38,200 --> 01:27:38,840
What over here?

1483
01:27:39,500 --> 01:27:40,340
There it is!

1484
01:27:40,420 --> 01:27:41,880
We are back home, people!

1485
01:27:42,600 --> 01:27:43,360
What a trip.

1486
01:27:44,680 --> 01:27:45,760
Unfortunately, no diamonds.

1487
01:27:45,860 --> 01:27:47,780
But I didn't really go into a cave, so...

1488
01:27:48,280 --> 01:27:49,540
I wouldn't call that a failure.

1489
01:27:50,440 --> 01:27:51,640
I would call it standard.

1490
01:27:54,840 --> 01:27:55,260
Iron...

1491
01:27:55,800 --> 01:27:56,740
Needs to be cooked!

1492
01:27:58,200 --> 01:27:58,620
Oh!

1493
01:27:59,480 --> 01:28:00,640
Yeah, just cooked that too.

1494
01:28:03,200 --> 01:28:04,120
We have gold.

1495
01:28:05,080 --> 01:28:06,500
Wait, what is, uh...

1496
01:28:06,500 --> 01:28:08,180
Oh, brass sheet and gold, they look similar.

1497
01:28:09,080 --> 01:28:09,740
I see.

1498
01:28:12,340 --> 01:28:13,720
Also have two smokers now.

1499
01:28:15,880 --> 01:28:16,680
Ominous bottle.

1500
01:28:16,820 --> 01:28:17,820
That's a random-ass item.

1501
01:28:18,080 --> 01:28:18,480
That goes in here.

1502
01:28:20,560 --> 01:28:23,280
I think I will relocate my chests inside the house today.

1503
01:28:23,780 --> 01:28:28,520
And get a preliminary setup going for item sorting.

1504
01:28:29,620 --> 01:28:31,000
Manual item sorting, mind you.

1505
01:28:33,620 --> 01:28:34,280
Um...

1506
01:28:35,100 --> 01:28:36,440
Give me this.

1507
01:28:37,580 --> 01:28:38,240
There.

1508
01:28:38,480 --> 01:28:38,800
There.

1509
01:28:39,140 --> 01:28:40,180
Oh, this needs to come off.

1510
01:28:41,880 --> 01:28:42,720
Come on.

1511
01:28:44,260 --> 01:28:45,780
Didn't I have a, uh...

1512
01:28:45,780 --> 01:28:46,440
Iron helmet?

1513
01:28:48,680 --> 01:28:49,540
Maybe not.

1514
01:28:50,220 --> 01:28:50,360
Oh.

1515
01:28:56,280 --> 01:28:56,940
Yeah.

1516
01:28:57,600 --> 01:28:58,020
Tank.

1517
01:28:59,160 --> 01:29:00,580
Honestly, I don't want this helmet.

1518
01:29:02,460 --> 01:29:03,420
Or this.

1519
01:29:05,300 --> 01:29:06,320
We can make paper.

1520
01:29:07,560 --> 01:29:08,540
Ah, but wait, wait, wait!

1521
01:29:09,120 --> 01:29:11,360
So, three sugarcane for three paper.

1522
01:29:11,640 --> 01:29:12,840
Can we do it better?

1523
01:29:16,740 --> 01:29:17,260
No.

1524
01:29:20,380 --> 01:29:20,900
Wait.

1525
01:29:21,780 --> 01:29:23,220
Book is cardboard.

1526
01:29:23,560 --> 01:29:23,820
Three...

1527
01:29:23,820 --> 01:29:24,720
Oh, it's just...

1528
01:29:24,720 --> 01:29:25,360
Uh, wait a minute.

1529
01:29:27,320 --> 01:29:27,840
Book.

1530
01:29:29,580 --> 01:29:30,380
Okay, yeah.

1531
01:29:30,480 --> 01:29:32,120
It's just cardboard or leather.

1532
01:29:32,400 --> 01:29:32,960
I see.

1533
01:29:33,480 --> 01:29:35,840
So we're not actually saving paper in any way there.

1534
01:29:36,780 --> 01:29:37,950
But I guess, uh...

1535
01:29:38,360 --> 01:29:38,600
Nah.

1536
01:29:39,600 --> 01:29:39,880
Okay.

1537
01:29:40,980 --> 01:29:41,440
Fine.

1538
01:29:42,260 --> 01:29:43,120
I'll make paper.

1539
01:29:44,100 --> 01:29:44,700
Twenty-seven.

1540
01:29:46,280 --> 01:29:48,360
And with that paper, we can make books.

1541
01:29:56,680 --> 01:29:58,140
That's not a lot of books, man.

1542
01:29:58,940 --> 01:29:59,400
That's...

1543
01:29:59,400 --> 01:29:59,560
Whew!

1544
01:30:00,600 --> 01:30:03,520
Yeah, we need to find a better way to make books.

1545
01:30:03,880 --> 01:30:04,600
For sure.

1546
01:30:05,400 --> 01:30:06,260
That was rough.

1547
01:30:06,420 --> 01:30:07,900
Only nine books from that whole trip.

1548
01:30:09,420 --> 01:30:10,200
That's crazy.

1549
01:30:10,720 --> 01:30:12,340
Did get 33 white wool, though.

1550
01:30:14,180 --> 01:30:14,940
And, you know what?

1551
01:30:14,940 --> 01:30:16,900
We probably need this to make an airplane, right?

1552
01:30:19,440 --> 01:30:19,880
So...

1553
01:30:19,880 --> 01:30:20,860
Good that we got it.

1554
01:30:23,780 --> 01:30:24,220
Apples...

1555
01:30:24,220 --> 01:30:24,740
Here.

1556
01:30:25,580 --> 01:30:26,780
I wanna grow potatoes!

1557
01:30:28,660 --> 01:30:30,540
Some of this becomes potato land now.

1558
01:30:30,620 --> 01:30:31,320
Half of it, actually.

1559
01:30:37,590 --> 01:30:39,390
I'll fill the rest up with potatoes later.

1560
01:30:43,990 --> 01:30:44,710
What else?

1561
01:30:44,970 --> 01:30:46,570
Oh, I should've probably done that.

1562
01:30:47,430 --> 01:30:49,310
Yeah, this axe is now dead to me.

1563
01:30:49,490 --> 01:30:49,730
Oh!

1564
01:30:50,030 --> 01:30:50,890
We can delete items!

1565
01:30:51,610 --> 01:30:52,090
Yeah!

1566
01:30:52,770 --> 01:30:53,210
Sick.

1567
01:30:54,650 --> 01:30:55,510
Fire protection.

1568
01:30:55,730 --> 01:30:56,910
I'm actually gonna keep these boots.

1569
01:30:56,990 --> 01:30:58,550
These boots are sick for the nether.

1570
01:30:59,390 --> 01:31:01,390
These are some great nether boots.

1571
01:31:04,150 --> 01:31:04,550
Uh...

1572
01:31:04,550 --> 01:31:05,390
I'll keep this too for now.

1573
01:31:06,850 --> 01:31:07,250
Yep.

1574
01:31:08,650 --> 01:31:09,050
Iron.

1575
01:31:10,890 --> 01:31:11,470
Cook it!

1576
01:31:12,890 --> 01:31:14,010
What else needs to be cooked?

1577
01:31:15,470 --> 01:31:15,790
Okay.

1578
01:31:22,760 --> 01:31:23,400
Some sand.

1579
01:31:24,720 --> 01:31:25,900
We have a lot of sand now.

1580
01:31:28,720 --> 01:31:29,520
Six diamonds.

1581
01:31:29,840 --> 01:31:31,240
I mean, we can make something out of that, right?

1582
01:31:32,400 --> 01:31:33,380
Chest piece or something?

1583
01:31:34,520 --> 01:31:35,120
No.

1584
01:31:35,760 --> 01:31:36,120
Next?

1585
01:31:36,540 --> 01:31:37,040
No!

1586
01:31:38,320 --> 01:31:38,920
Boots?

1587
01:31:39,180 --> 01:31:39,740
Yes!

1588
01:31:41,120 --> 01:31:42,260
But is it worth it?

1589
01:31:46,130 --> 01:31:46,730
Yeah.

1590
01:31:46,970 --> 01:31:48,110
My boots are about to be destroyed.

1591
01:31:49,490 --> 01:31:50,210
Do it.

1592
01:31:52,390 --> 01:31:53,750
Cover me with diamonds.

1593
01:31:54,070 --> 01:31:56,030
Although, I wouldn't call that covering, but...

1594
01:31:56,290 --> 01:31:56,390
Sure.

1595
01:32:00,920 --> 01:32:02,220
I have 14 arrows.

1596
01:32:02,720 --> 01:32:03,760
That's just not good enough.

1597
01:32:05,260 --> 01:32:06,320
I need that bow.

1598
01:32:09,000 --> 01:32:10,020
Do I not have any string?

1599
01:32:10,840 --> 01:32:11,580
Yeah, I...

1600
01:32:11,580 --> 01:32:13,120
Dude, I need to go caving so bad.

1601
01:32:13,820 --> 01:32:14,900
To get that diamond.

1602
01:32:16,520 --> 01:32:16,900
And...

1603
01:32:16,900 --> 01:32:17,260
Wait, wait, wait.

1604
01:32:17,440 --> 01:32:20,780
So, to get the diamonds, I gotta go find diamonds.

1605
01:32:20,960 --> 01:32:24,020
And the reason I get diamonds is to get diamond armor so I can go caving.

1606
01:32:26,740 --> 01:32:28,480
Or just survival in general, I guess.

1607
01:32:28,560 --> 01:32:30,160
But I also need to enchant my shit.

1608
01:32:30,640 --> 01:32:32,870
Because I'd rather go caving with an enchanted pickaxe.

1609
01:32:34,510 --> 01:32:36,730
So to do that, I need books, right?

1610
01:32:37,130 --> 01:32:39,530
And I need enchanting table.

1611
01:32:39,830 --> 01:32:40,470
Have I done that?

1612
01:32:40,630 --> 01:32:41,370
Enchanting table.

1613
01:32:44,010 --> 01:32:44,890
Enchanting table.

1614
01:32:47,010 --> 01:32:48,190
I don't think I have!

1615
01:32:48,450 --> 01:32:49,210
Let's make it.

1616
01:32:51,830 --> 01:32:53,250
Obsidian, diamonds, and book.

1617
01:32:53,390 --> 01:32:53,570
Okay.

1618
01:32:56,050 --> 01:32:56,570
Fuck.

1619
01:32:56,570 --> 01:32:57,930
I don't have any obsidian.

1620
01:33:01,490 --> 01:33:01,970
Shit.

1621
01:33:03,190 --> 01:33:03,670
Ah!

1622
01:33:05,750 --> 01:33:06,530
Oh my god.

1623
01:33:06,670 --> 01:33:07,130
I feel like...

1624
01:33:07,130 --> 01:33:09,070
Why is progression so hard right now?

1625
01:33:09,450 --> 01:33:10,950
I'm usually way better at this.

1626
01:33:11,690 --> 01:33:15,050
I feel like I'm being limited by external forces.

1627
01:33:17,670 --> 01:33:19,110
It's not me who's doing it.

1628
01:33:20,130 --> 01:33:21,090
It's just happening.

1629
01:33:22,490 --> 01:33:23,930
Oh wait, we have more sugarcane.

1630
01:33:25,770 --> 01:33:26,290
Nether.

1631
01:33:27,730 --> 01:33:28,250
Book!

1632
01:33:30,450 --> 01:33:31,290
Wait, paper.

1633
01:33:32,870 --> 01:33:33,790
And then book.

1634
01:33:35,470 --> 01:33:36,510
63, baby!

1635
01:33:38,930 --> 01:33:39,450
Yeah!

1636
01:33:39,990 --> 01:33:40,530
Okay, okay.

1637
01:33:40,530 --> 01:33:41,350
We're actually cooking now.

1638
01:33:42,770 --> 01:33:44,430
I think we may be onto something here.

1639
01:33:44,770 --> 01:33:46,150
And now, bookcase.

1640
01:33:47,790 --> 01:33:48,950
It's just wood!

1641
01:33:49,780 --> 01:33:50,210
Easy.

1642
01:33:55,250 --> 01:33:55,680
Case.

1643
01:33:56,120 --> 01:33:56,780
That's 10!

1644
01:33:57,460 --> 01:33:58,420
Not bad!

1645
01:33:58,900 --> 01:34:01,160
Now we need to find some obsidian.

1646
01:34:02,580 --> 01:34:04,460
Let me actually do a quick...

1647
01:34:04,460 --> 01:34:06,580
I'm gonna quickly scan the land.

1648
01:34:22,780 --> 01:34:23,260
Bip!

1649
01:34:25,740 --> 01:34:27,140
We got lava.

1650
01:34:32,030 --> 01:34:32,890
Oh!

1651
01:34:33,450 --> 01:34:34,050
Whoa!

1652
01:34:34,210 --> 01:34:34,950
That broke fast.

1653
01:34:35,790 --> 01:34:36,450
What?

1654
01:34:36,830 --> 01:34:38,490
Wasn't that at like 70%?

1655
01:34:39,950 --> 01:34:40,750
Fucking useless.

1656
01:34:41,750 --> 01:34:42,210
Wow.

1657
01:34:45,650 --> 01:34:46,370
Give me that.

1658
01:34:47,010 --> 01:34:47,650
Here we go!

1659
01:34:50,190 --> 01:34:50,850
Quick sleep.

1660
01:35:00,790 --> 01:35:01,490
I'm lost.

1661
01:35:02,050 --> 01:35:02,650
No, I'm not.

1662
01:35:05,170 --> 01:35:07,010
Wait, there was lava here the entire time?

1663
01:35:08,310 --> 01:35:09,330
That's kinda crazy.

1664
01:35:13,080 --> 01:35:15,740
I could've sworn there was lava on the other side though, of the lake.

1665
01:35:16,380 --> 01:35:17,960
Like, I feel like I remember that.

1666
01:35:25,330 --> 01:35:25,970
Weeeeee!

1667
01:35:35,590 --> 01:35:36,750
I needed three.

1668
01:35:37,070 --> 01:35:37,690
No, four.

1669
01:35:38,130 --> 01:35:38,550
Ooh!

1670
01:35:38,890 --> 01:35:40,070
I almost went in!

1671
01:35:40,530 --> 01:35:41,610
Jesus Christ!

1672
01:35:42,750 --> 01:35:43,390
Wow!

1673
01:35:53,150 --> 01:35:53,970
One more.

1674
01:36:03,510 --> 01:36:04,470
Oi, oi, oi!

1675
01:36:05,890 --> 01:36:07,370
I got what I came for.

1676
01:36:07,470 --> 01:36:08,170
Oopsie daisy!

1677
01:36:09,350 --> 01:36:09,730
Sorry!

1678
01:36:12,270 --> 01:36:13,290
I'm gonna snip.

1679
01:36:14,350 --> 01:36:14,910
Hey!

1680
01:36:17,310 --> 01:36:17,870
Hey!

1681
01:36:18,050 --> 01:36:18,730
I can mill that!

1682
01:36:19,090 --> 01:36:19,490
Sick!

1683
01:36:22,190 --> 01:36:22,990
Fuck yeah!

1684
01:36:23,170 --> 01:36:23,890
I need greenery.

1685
01:36:26,550 --> 01:36:27,990
Let me put some greenery here.

1686
01:36:28,450 --> 01:36:29,150
